   "text": "The run ended with reward 0.0 and a TrialBudgetExhaustedError after 102 episodes [R0M.trace_lab]. The budget ran out after many turns, which fits a request ceiling.\n\nThe model typed all seven methods in place with one heredoc edit, but that edit uppercases the segment and index values: \"params = {\"index\": segment.upper()}\" [T0B83:<RANGE>params = {\"index\": segment.upper()}</RANGE>]. It does the same in annual_reports: \"params = {\"index\": segment.upper(), \"symbol\": symbol.upper()}\" [T0B83:<RANGE>params = {\"index\": segment.upper(), \"symbol\": symbol.upper()}</RANGE>]. The task asks for `index` set from `segment` and \"call `/annual-reports` with `index=segment`\" [T0B0:<RANGE>call `/annual-reports` with `index=segment`</RANGE>], so it does not ask for uppercasing.\n\nThe model's own mock tests printed \"{'index': 'EQUITIES'}\" [T0B112:<RANGE>{'index': 'EQUITIES'}</RANGE>]. The model never questioned this value.\n\nThe model called mark_task_complete [T0B125:<RANGE>mark_task_complete()</RANGE>]. The harness asked for confirmation: \"If so, include \"task_complete\": true in your JSON response again.\" [T0B126:<RANGE>If so, include \"task_complete\": true in your JSON response again.</RANGE>]. The model never sent that confirmation. Instead it ran echo commands such as \"echo \"task verified complete\"\" [T0B127:<RANGE>echo \"task verified complete\"</RANGE>] and kept doing so until the budget ran out.\n\nAfter a context handoff, the model re-verified the code and resumed echo-done turns through the end of the transcript.",
